  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the living conditions of affected populations (IDPs and returnees) in the Central African Republic through multi-sectoral assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2013, the Central African Republic&#x2019;s population has faced chronic structural challenges and shocks that increase their vulnerability. These shocks include insecurity caused by clashes opposing armed elements for the control of territories and resources, epidemics, inter-community tensions, and disasters (floods and fires). The security situation remained volatile throughout 2023, punctuated by continuous clashes between the Central African armed forces (FACA) and armed groups.Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to improving the living conditions of disaster-affected populations through data collection/information sharing, flexible and rapid Shelter/non-food item (NFI) response and shelter reconstruction in return/relocation areas, and development of livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
